course: dictionary
lesson: 16188
title: The zenith: the highest point
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The zenith is the highest point you can reach. In the sky, it is the point directly above your head. «At noon on a clear day, the Sun was almost at its zenith.» The Sun was as high as it could go, right over the children's heads.
explain: The word can also mean the best time of something. «The team reached its zenith when it won the cup.» The clue is won the cup: the team was at its most successful, so zenith means the peak.
explain: Its opposite is the nadir, the lowest point, which is directly under your feet. The phrase «from zenith to nadir» means from the very top all the way to the very bottom.
fact: The zenith is the point in the sky directly above your head.
fact: Near the equator, the Sun can be at the zenith at noon on some days.
fact: «Zenith» can also mean the highest point a heavenly body, such as the Sun, reaches in the sky.
fact: In history, «at its zenith» means at its strongest: «The Roman Empire was at its zenith in the second century.»
fact: The opposite of zenith is nadir, the point directly under your feet.
exercise: «The Sun was at its zenith at noon.» Where was the Sun? | *Directly above your head | Hidden behind the hills | Under your feet | Low on the horizon at sunset
exercise: «The garden was at its zenith in June, full of colour.» What does zenith mean here? | *The peak, the most beautiful and successful time | The very start of the year | A cold, empty time | The end of the summer
exercise: Which word is the opposite of zenith? | *nadir | peak | noon | summit
test: «The city was at its zenith when the trade ships filled its harbour.» What does zenith mean here? | Its busy harbour, where ships park | Its darkest, quietest time | *Its most powerful, successful time | Its very first day
test: Where would you look to see the zenith at noon? | Down at your feet | *Straight up, overhead | Towards the horizon at sunset | In a mirror on the wall
exam: «The rocket soared to its zenith, then fell back to the ground.» What is the zenith of the rocket's flight? | The loud noise of its engine | The moment it landed | The launch pad on the ground | *The highest point it reached
